            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Before the new one: say the Malayalam for a waiting room, then the Malayalam for a roadside food stall."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 1,
          "type": "input",
          "title": "You'll want to know: എംബസി",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "എംബസി — embasi — \"an embassy\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "വിസയ്ക്കായി അവൾ എംബസിയിൽ പോയി. visaykkāyi avaḷ embasiyil pōyi. She went to the embassy for a visa."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Each country has one embassy in the capital, and a consulate in some other cities."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "എംബസി (embasi) was borrowed from English embassy, the office of a foreign government in the capital."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
          "type": "notice",
          "title": "What you've built",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "One more word for getting around."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
